  "beats": [
    {
      "beat_id": "B00",
      "act": "cold open",
      "narration_text": "Merhaba — this is Liam, in for Bear. Ever notice a model pauses, then the words just stream out fast? That gap has a name: the KV-cache.",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "claude \"explain why LLM generation speeds up after the first token — the KV-cache mechanism\"",
            "topic": "SYSTEMS · KV-CACHE",
            "segment": "Claude, Cached.",
            "greeting": "Merhaba, Liam",
            "runningText": "tracing prefill vs decode…",
            "output": [
              "Prefill: compute the whole prompt at once",
              "Decode: reuse what's cached, add one token",
              "Cache grows with context — the real cost"
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B00.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B00.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.18,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B00.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-31T10:06:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "executive summary",
      "narration_text": "Attention needs the Key and Value vectors of every past token. Those don't change once computed, so cache them. Each new token only computes its own K and V, then reuses everything before it.",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B01_BLUF",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.83,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B01_BLUF",
        "at": "2026-08-31T10:06:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "framework",
      "narration_text": "Every token produces a Key and a Value vector per layer. To generate the next token, attention compares its Query against all previous Keys. Compute those once — they're valid forever. The future never changes the past.",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 17,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B02_Framework",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.89,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B02_Framework",
        "at": "2026-08-31T10:06:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "worked example (prefill)",
      "narration_text": "This is why the pause happens up front: prefill computes Key and Value for the whole prompt in one big parallel pass. Every token's cache entry lands at once — that's the 'thinking' delay you feel.",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B03_Prefill",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.9,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B03_Prefill",
        "at": "2026-08-31T10:06:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "worked example (decode)",
      "narration_text": "Decode adds one token at a time. Its Query attends to every cached Key — nothing recomputed. That single cheap step, repeated, is the fast streaming you actually see.",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 15,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B04_Decode",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.18,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B04_Decode",
        "at": "2026-08-31T10:06:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "falsifiability",
      "narration_text": "The catch: the cache grows with every token, times every layer, times every attention head. Long conversations mean a bigger cache sitting in memory — that's the real reason very long contexts get slow and expensive.",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 17,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B05_Growth",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.6,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B05_Growth",
        "at": "2026-08-31T10:06:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "verdict",
      "narration_text": "Verdict: the KV-cache is why decode is cheap and prefill is not. It trades compute for memory — each token's cache entry sits around for the rest of the conversation. That's exactly why paged attention and cache eviction exist.",
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 17,
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "claude \"verdict: what does the KV-cache actually trade off?\"",
            "topic": "SYSTEMS · KV-CACHE",
            "segment": "Claude, Cached.",
            "greeting": "The verdict,",
            "runningText": "checking the mechanism…",
            "output": [
              "Decode is cheap: one new K/V, attend to the rest",
              "Prefill is not: the whole prompt, one big pass",
              "Trade-off: compute for memory — the cache never shrinks itself"
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B06.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
